[HEADING=1]Ubuntu 26.04 + Angie beats CentMinMod on the same EPYC host — XenForo 2.3.13, PHP 8.2–8.5[/HEADING]

[B]Same AMD EPYC 4245P (6C/12T, 30 GiB, 2×894 GB NVMe), same XenForo dataset, same wrk 4.1.0 method as the AlmaLinux 10 + CentMinMod run. The Ubuntu stack is tuned by [ICODE]setup.sh[/ICODE] 1.21.24 + [ICODE]server-configs-nginx[/ICODE] 1.6.38.[/B]

[HEADING=2]TL;DR[/HEADING]

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Stack (PHP 8.2–8.5 avg)[/TH][TH]Metric[/TH][TH]CentMinMod[/TH][TH]Ubuntu + Angie[/TH][TH]Delta[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]3 — Redis + page cache[/TD][TD]Guest cached[/TD][TD]157,957[/TD][TD][B]390,232[/B][/TD][TD][B]+147.1 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]4 — + Anubis[/TD][TD]Guest cached[/TD][TD]59,958[/TD][TD][B]68,725[/B][/TD][TD][B]+14.6 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]1 — Plain[/TD][TD]Guest bypass[/TD][TD]596[/TD][TD][B]775[/B][/TD][TD][B]+30.1 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]3 — Redis + page cache[/TD][TD]Member home[/TD][TD]542[/TD][TD][B]747[/B][/TD][TD][B]+37.9 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]3 — Redis + page cache[/TD][TD]Member thread[/TD][TD]694[/TD][TD][B]838[/B][/TD][TD][B]+20.7 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[B]Every comparable cell is above CentMinMod.[/B] The largest single difference is a TLS setting: [ICODE]ssl_buffer_size 1400[/ICODE] split each cached page into ~11 TLS records, [ICODE]16k[/ICODE] sends it as one. On the same page and TLS stack that alone moved the cached guest tier from [B]151,438 to 442,765 req/s[/B].

